## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within
`requires-python` option in [pyproject.toml](pyproject.toml).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].

## Project design concepts

WTS is a solution that allows simulating the UEs and Core Network for testing eNB.

It launches both eGate and eDaemon processes.
eGate is a user interface that allows controlling the simulators and eDaemon launches all the simulators defined in configuration.

Overview of the solution you can find [here][5].

## How to configure WTS manually

To configure WTS you need proper configuration files. You can find them in [topology-configs][6] repository.
Each topology has its own folder with configuration files related to specific release.
Inside each folder you can find `config.yaml` file where you can find details about which configuration file is the default one.

Once you have the proper configuration, reserve the testline in CM.
Start WTS application, connect to EGATE instance via telnet and configure your environment by running

`cfg file=/home/ute/testline_init_results/execution/configs/topology_configs/<configuration file path>`.

Sometimes EGATE needs to be restarted to apply the new configuration. You can do this by running `reset` in EGATE terminal.

## How to start WTS manually

```
cd /opt/iphy/latest
sudo ./edaemon --port 22222
./egate --port 20000
telnet 0 20000
```

